  "notes": "Huey is an almost entirely greyscale, desktop-app-like pivot tool: no brand color at all. Axis shelves are rounded pill chips (r 15px) in full-width rounded input-like rows, each pill carrying tiny line icons (totals toggle, move to other axis, remove, < > reorder). The result grid uses monospace font with right-aligned numbers, light grey header cells, and ditto marks (〃) instead of repeating row/column labels. Query state is encoded entirely in the URL hash (base64 JSON). Toolbar shows live tuple counts for rows (15) and columns (13). Sidebar tabs are pill-shaped (r 18px) with the active one darker grey."
